00:17:33,319 --> 00:17:34,320
Jay: YOU GUYS DID
A GOOD JOB,

467
00:17:34,320 --> 00:17:36,489
BUT YOU'RE GONNA
HAVE TO COOK THE DINNER.

468
00:17:36,489 --> 00:17:37,490
CONGRATULATIONS.

469
00:17:37,490 --> 00:17:38,491
YOU DID A GREAT JOB.

470
00:17:38,491 --> 00:17:39,525
HAVE A FUN DINNER.

471
00:17:39,525 --> 00:17:41,527
Catie: LET ME JUST SAY
I'M REALLY BAD.

472
00:17:41,527 --> 00:17:43,529
YOU GUYS MIGHT WANT
ME TO DO THE SALAD.

473
00:17:43,529 --> 00:17:45,898
Heather: IT WOULDN'T HAVE
BOTHERED ME WHEN YOANNA CHOSE

474
00:17:45,898 --> 00:17:50,570
WHO SHE GOT TO PICK OUT IF
SHE DIDN'T REACH FOR ME

475
00:17:50,570 --> 00:17:52,805
AND LOOK AT ME
FIRST, AND THEN TURN AWAY

476
00:17:52,805 --> 00:17:55,074
AND PICK APRIL.

477
00:17:55,508 --> 00:17:57,009
NO ONE'S GONNA BE
THERE FOR YOU.

478
00:17:57,009 --> 00:17:59,612
THAT'S WHAT I LEARNED.

479
00:17:59,612 --> 00:18:02,181
Shandi: I AM GETTING WARM.

480
00:18:02,181 --> 00:18:04,283
IT IS SO HOT IN HERE.

481
00:18:04,283 --> 00:18:05,384
LIKE, I START SWEATING.

482
00:18:05,384 --> 00:18:07,086
I FEEL DIZZY.

483
00:18:07,086 --> 00:18:08,554
Camille: SHANDI,
YOU OKAY?

484
00:18:08,554 --> 00:18:09,555
Xiomara: YOU OKAY?

485
00:18:09,555 --> 00:18:10,556
SHANDI!

486
00:18:10,556 --> 00:18:11,557
YOU'RE NOT OKAY.

487
00:18:11,557 --> 00:18:13,392
Sara: OH, MY GOD!

488
00:18:13,392 --> 00:18:15,394
I LOOK OVER, AND
SHANDI'S COLLAPSED

489
00:18:15,394 --> 00:18:16,629
ON THE GROUND.

490
00:18:18,631 --> 00:18:22,935
Catie: HELP HER.

491
00:18:22,935 --> 00:18:24,904
Jenascia: IT WAS A COMPLETE
AND TOTAL NIGHTMARE.

492
00:18:28,641 --> 00:18:30,843
Xiomara: I'M SO SCARED
FOR SHANDI.

493
00:18:30,843 --> 00:18:33,646
I'M SCARED.

494
00:18:40,820 --> 00:18:46,258
(siren wailing)

495
00:18:46,258 --> 00:18:50,062
Catie: THERE'S NOTHING
WE CAN HELP.

496
00:18:50,062 --> 00:18:52,064
Yoanna: I KNEW SHANDI'S
BLOOD SUGAR WAS LOW.

497
00:18:52,064 --> 00:18:54,467
I RAN TO MY BAG TO GET
HER SOME PEANUT BUTTER,

498
00:18:54,467 --> 00:18:56,135
A PIECE OF CHOCOLATE OR CANDY
TO RAISE HER BLOOD SUGAR.

499
00:18:59,171 --> 00:19:00,773
Shandi: IT WAS REALLY
SCARY.

500
00:19:00,773 --> 00:19:02,141
I'VE NEVER
GOTTEN SO HOT

501
00:19:02,141 --> 00:19:05,211
TO THE POINT OF WHERE I
WAS JUST DIZZY AND NAUSEOUS,

502
00:19:05,211 --> 00:19:07,246
AND, LIKE, I
COULDN'T BREATHE.

503
00:19:07,246 --> 00:19:08,447
Jenascia: YOU FEEL BETTER?

504
00:19:08,447 --> 00:19:09,815
Shandi: YEAH,
MUCH BETTER.

505
00:19:09,815 --> 00:19:13,352
I NEED TO MAKE THE TIME TO
GET SLEEP AND EAT AS MUCH

506
00:19:13,352 --> 00:19:15,621
AS I CAN.

507
00:19:16,188 --> 00:19:17,189
I PASSED OUT.

508
00:19:17,189 --> 00:19:19,525
I DON'T WANT IT
TO HAPPEN AGAIN.

509
00:19:26,699 --> 00:19:28,668
Heather: A GIRL PASSED
OUT TODAY.

510
00:19:28,668 --> 00:19:30,036
IT'S SO STRESSFUL.

511
00:19:30,036 --> 00:19:31,804
AND I'M SO SAD.

512
00:19:31,804 --> 00:19:34,540
I WANT TO MODEL, BUT,
LIKE, IF THIS IS WHAT

513
00:19:34,540 --> 00:19:36,876
IT TAKES, I'D RATHER
BE HAPPY,

514
00:19:36,876 --> 00:19:39,011
BUT, HEY, I GOTTA GO 'CAUSE
WE'RE SERVING DINNER

515
00:19:39,011 --> 00:19:40,079
RIGHT NOW, SO...

516
00:19:40,079 --> 00:19:41,080
Heather's mother: I love you.

517
00:19:41,080 --> 00:19:42,548
Heather: I LOVE
YOU, MOM.

518
00:19:42,548 --> 00:19:43,749
Xiomara: HI, GUYS.

519
00:19:43,749 --> 00:19:45,084
Yoanna: SMELLS REALLY GOOD.

520
00:19:45,084 --> 00:19:46,786
I HAVE BEEN WANTING TO WIN AT
SOMETHING, AND TODAY,

521
00:19:46,786 --> 00:19:48,087
IT FINALLY HAPPENED.

522
00:19:48,087 --> 00:19:50,756
I'M JAZZED THAT CAMILLE'S GONNA,
YOU KNOW, COOK A MEAL

523
00:19:50,756 --> 00:19:51,791
FOR ME AND MY GUESTS.

524
00:19:51,791 --> 00:19:54,260
I THINK IT MIGHT DO
HER SOME GOOD.

525
00:19:54,527 --> 00:19:58,297
♪♪♪

526
00:20:03,335 --> 00:20:04,603
Catie: WHO IS COMING?

527
00:20:04,603 --> 00:20:06,172
Sara: I DON'T KNOW.

528
00:20:06,172 --> 00:20:08,340
April: I DON'T KNOW, EITHER.

529
00:20:08,340 --> 00:20:09,442
A.J.: WHOO, MAN,

530
00:20:09,442 --> 00:20:12,211
LOOK AT THIS PLACE.

531
00:20:12,211 --> 00:20:13,846
Mike R.: HELLO.

532
00:20:13,846 --> 00:20:15,181
Yoanna: HEY,
WHAT'S GOING ON?

533
00:20:15,181 --> 00:20:16,182
A.J.: WHAT'S UP?

534
00:20:16,182 --> 00:20:16,782
HOW'S IT GOING?

535
00:20:17,183 --> 00:20:18,684
Yoanna: OUR GUESTS HAVE JUST
ARRIVED,

536
00:20:18,684 --> 00:20:21,687
AND IT'S THE ADAMS FROM THE
GARDEN OF EDEN PHOTO SHOOT.

537
00:20:23,723 --> 00:20:25,658
April: IT'S JUST GREAT TO HAVE
SOME KIND OF MALE

538
00:20:25,658 --> 00:20:27,093
IN THE HOUSE.

539
00:20:27,093 --> 00:20:30,062
Yoanna: SO HOW'D YOU GUYS GET
STARTED, LIKE, IN MODELING?

540
00:20:30,062 --> 00:20:31,363
IMG JUST SIGNED YOU UP?

541
00:20:31,363 --> 00:20:33,599
Mike S.: YEAH, BEEN OVER HERE
FOR, LIKE, FIVE MONTHS.

542
00:20:33,599 --> 00:20:34,600
Yoanna: ARE YOU CONSTANTLY
BOOKED,

543
00:20:34,600 --> 00:20:35,835
OR HOW DOES IT WORK?

544
00:20:35,835 --> 00:20:37,837
I JUST WANTED TO KIND OF GET THE
INSIDE SCOOP ON IMG

545
00:20:37,837 --> 00:20:40,172
AND PICK HIS BRAINS ON
HOW TO BE A SUCCESS

546
00:20:40,172 --> 00:20:42,608
IF I WERE TO
WIN THAT CONTRACT.

547
00:20:43,375 --> 00:20:47,446
TWIGGY, CAN I GET SOME
MORE, UM, LETTUCE?

548
00:20:47,446 --> 00:20:48,748
DO YOU MIND?

549
00:20:48,748 --> 00:20:50,750
Jenascia: DO WE HAVE
ANY EXTRA VEGETABLES?

550
00:20:50,750 --> 00:20:52,752
Catie: HERE. PEOPLE HAVE SOME
OVER HERE THAT WE CAN JUST

551
00:20:52,752 --> 00:20:57,089
CHOP UP FOR
HER OR SOMETHING.

552
00:20:58,124 --> 00:21:00,326
Camille: CATIE DECIDED TO
TAKE IT UPON HERSELF

553
00:21:00,326 --> 00:21:01,927
AND USE MY TOMATOES
AND USE MY LETTUCE

554
00:21:01,927 --> 00:21:03,929
TO MAKE YOANNA A
SALAD WITHOUT ASKING ME.

555
00:21:03,929 --> 00:21:06,966
MY DECISION, LIKE, NOT TO USE MY
VEGETABLES

556
00:21:06,966 --> 00:21:08,834
'CAUSE I HAVE TO EAT TOMORROW
MYSELF, WHEN I HAVE TO PAY--

557
00:21:08,834 --> 00:21:10,269
Catie: I'LL GO AND BUY YOU SOME
TONIGHT.

558
00:21:10,269 --> 00:21:11,270
I'M SORRY.

559
00:21:11,270 --> 00:21:12,438
Camille: WELL, YOU
SHOULDN'T

560
00:21:12,438 --> 00:21:15,040
HAVE DONE THAT WITHOUT
ASKING ME FIRST, CATIE.

561
00:21:15,040 --> 00:21:16,575
Catie: IT'S NOT THAT BIG
OF A DEAL, CAMILLE.

562
00:21:16,575 --> 00:21:18,244
IT'S A STINKIN' TOMATO

563
00:21:18,244 --> 00:21:19,812
AND, LIKE, SIX PIECES

564
00:21:19,812 --> 00:21:21,313
OF LETTUCE.

565
00:21:21,313 --> 00:21:22,248
GET OVER IT.

566
00:21:23,482 --> 00:21:26,619
Yoanna: THAT'S RIGHT. YEAH.

567
00:21:27,820 --> 00:21:29,822
Heather: YOANNA NOT PICKING ME

568
00:21:29,822 --> 00:21:31,824
KIND OF BOTHERED ME, HAVING TO
SERVE HER FOOD.

569
00:21:31,824 --> 00:21:34,660
DOES ANYBODY NEED ANY MORE
WATER?

570
00:21:35,394 --> 00:21:36,762
WHEN I WAS
SERVING THEM,

571
00:21:36,762 --> 00:21:38,464
THEY SIT THERE AND IGNORE YOU.

572
00:21:38,464 --> 00:21:39,832
I MADE YOU A DINNER,

573
00:21:39,832 --> 00:21:42,968
AND YOU'RE GONNA TREAT ME
WITH THIS KIND OF RESPECT?

574
00:21:44,236 --> 00:21:47,339
I JUST COULDN'T
TAKE IT ANYMORE.

575
00:21:48,107 --> 00:21:50,342
YOU KNOW, I TRY TO
TALK TO SOME PEOPLE,

576
00:21:50,342 --> 00:21:52,044
AND THEY, LIKE,
DON'T EVEN WANT

577
00:21:52,044 --> 00:21:53,045
TO LOOK AT ME WHEN
I TALK TO THEM.

578
00:21:53,045 --> 00:21:54,046
THEY DON'T EVEN WANT TO,

579
00:21:54,046 --> 00:21:55,181
YOU KNOW...

580
00:21:55,181 --> 00:21:56,315
Catie: ACKNOWLEDGE
THAT YOU'RE SPEAKING?

581
00:21:56,315 --> 00:21:57,316
Heather: ACKNOWLEDGE THAT I'M
SPEAKING.

582
00:21:57,316 --> 00:21:58,317
YOU NOTICED THAT?

583
00:21:58,317 --> 00:21:59,051
Catie: WE ALL GO THROUGH IT.

584
00:21:59,051 --> 00:22:00,119
YOU WANT TO
START WALKING BACK?

585
00:22:00,119 --> 00:22:01,153
Heather: YEAH.

586
00:22:01,153 --> 00:22:02,988
I CAN'T BELIEVE I JUST
SPILLED MY GUTS.

587
00:22:03,122 --> 00:22:04,757
Catie: THAT'S THE ONE
THING I LIKE ABOUT YOU.

588
00:22:06,959 --> 00:22:09,762
Heather: CATIE SEEMS TO
UNDERSTAND ME, AND IT MAKES

589
00:22:09,762 --> 00:22:14,066
ME HAPPY THAT SOMEONE ELSE
FEELS THE SAME WAY I DO,

590
00:22:14,066 --> 00:22:16,101
THAT I'M NOT ALONE IN THIS
HOUSE.

591
00:22:16,101 --> 00:22:17,670
Mercedes: WE GOT
MAIL, YOU GUYS!

592
00:22:17,670 --> 00:22:20,272
Xiomara: WE GOT MAIL?

593
00:22:20,706 --> 00:22:22,107
WHAT'S IT SAY?

594
00:22:23,142 --> 00:22:24,143
Xiomara: "VENUSTRAPHOBIA...

595
00:22:24,143 --> 00:22:25,177
Camille: "VENUSTRAPHOBIA...

596
00:22:25,177 --> 00:22:26,212
Both: "THE FEAR OF BEAUTIFUL
WOMEN.

597
00:22:26,212 --> 00:22:29,481
OPHIDIOPHOBIA-- THE
FEAR OF SNAKES.

598
00:22:29,481 --> 00:22:31,851
ALGOPHOBIA--THE
FEAR OF PAIN.

599
00:22:31,851 --> 00:22:32,885
WHAT ARE YOU AFRAID OF?

600
00:22:32,885 --> 00:22:34,620
WE'LL FIND
OUT TOMORROW.

601
00:22:34,620 --> 00:22:36,722
BE READY AT 7 IN
THE MORNING ."

602
00:22:36,722 --> 00:22:39,091
Catie: TYRA MAIL WAS TALKING
ABOUT A PHOTO SHOOT

603
00:22:39,091 --> 00:22:40,092
THAT HAD SOMETHING
TO DO WITH

604
00:22:40,092 --> 00:22:42,027
PEOPLE FEARS AND PHOBIAS,

605
00:22:42,027 --> 00:22:43,462
BUT I THINK FEAR
IS A COMPLETE

606
00:22:43,462 --> 00:22:45,564
WASTE OF EMOTIONS AND TIME.

607
00:22:45,731 --> 00:22:47,900
♪♪♪

608
00:22:51,637 --> 00:22:53,205
Shandi: I WAS ABLE TO GET
A LITTLE BIT OF SLEEP

609
00:22:53,205 --> 00:22:54,206
AND EAT SOMETHING,

610
00:22:54,206 --> 00:22:55,574
SO I FEEL TONS BETTER.

611
00:22:57,943 --> 00:22:59,612
Catie: I HAVE NO
IDEA WHAT WE'RE GONNA DO

612
00:22:59,612 --> 00:23:01,447
WHEN WE GET TO
THE LOCATION.

613
00:23:01,447 --> 00:23:05,985
♪♪♪

614
00:23:05,985 --> 00:23:08,254
Mercedes: I MEAN, DO WE
REALLY NEED THE AMBULANCE?

615
00:23:08,254 --> 00:23:09,655
Sara: WHY ARE WE IN THE
BOONDOCKS

616
00:23:09,655 --> 00:23:11,257
OF THE BUILDING?

617
00:23:13,292 --> 00:23:15,394
Catie: ONCE WE WALK
INTO THE BUILDING,

618
00:23:15,394 --> 00:23:17,630
WE AUTOMATICALLY THINK IT HAS
SOMETHING TO DO WITH DEATH.

619
00:23:20,032 --> 00:23:21,567
THERE'S, LIKE, DEAD
BIRDS EVERYWHERE,

620
00:23:21,567 --> 00:23:24,904
AND PAINT'S CHIPPING OFF.

621
00:23:24,904 --> 00:23:25,838
Jay: GIRLS, COME IN.

622
00:23:26,572 --> 00:23:29,775
Catie: WHEN WE GOT TO THE
PLACE WHERE JAY WAS,

623
00:23:29,775 --> 00:23:32,511
I SEE THESE HUGE HOLES.

624
00:23:33,679 --> 00:23:35,180
VERY TERRIFIED OF THAT.

625
00:23:35,180 --> 00:23:36,415
(banging)

626
00:23:36,415 --> 00:23:37,917
Catie: BECAUSE MY ULTIMATE
FEAR IN LIFE IS FALLING

627
00:23:37,917 --> 00:23:38,918
TO MY DEATH.

628
00:23:38,918 --> 00:23:40,319
Jay: GOOD MORNING, GIRLS.

629
00:23:40,319 --> 00:23:43,122
TOP MODELS TRAVEL ALL OVER THE
WORLD TO EXOTIC LOCATIONS

630
00:23:43,122 --> 00:23:44,456
AND WEIRD LOCATIONS,

631
00:23:44,456 --> 00:23:47,426
JUST LIKE THIS, SO TODAY WE'RE
GONNA CREATE AN ACTION

632
00:23:47,426 --> 00:23:48,594
FASHION EDITORIAL,

633
00:23:48,594 --> 00:23:50,129
WEARING INCREDIBLE DESIGNS

634
00:23:50,129 --> 00:23:52,464
FROM LAUNDRY BY SHELLI SEGAL.

635
00:23:52,464 --> 00:23:56,969
NOW THERE'S ONE
TWIST TO THIS SHOOT.

636
00:23:56,969 --> 00:24:00,606
WE ARE GOING TO SUSPEND
YOU FROM THIS LEDGE

637
00:24:00,606 --> 00:24:05,210
AND SHOOT YOU GUYS
HANGING OVER THIS HOLE.

638
00:24:05,577 --> 00:24:07,579
Catie: I DON'T WANT TO
DO THIS.

639
00:24:07,579 --> 00:24:09,415
AND I'M VERY SCARED.

640
00:24:09,415 --> 00:24:10,983
I DON'T WANT TO DIE.

641
00:24:10,983 --> 00:24:12,651
Jay: COOL? PSYCHED?

642
00:24:12,651 --> 00:24:13,619
MEET YOU DOWNSTAIRS.

643
00:24:16,422 --> 00:24:20,059
♪♪♪

644
00:24:28,934 --> 00:24:30,169
Richard: I DID ONE
WHERE THEY HUNG ME OUT

645
00:24:30,169 --> 00:24:31,603
OF THE HELICOPTER.

646
00:24:31,603 --> 00:24:32,871
I'LL JUMP OFF ANYTHING.

647
00:24:34,540 --> 00:24:35,841
Catie: I JUST WISH MY DAD WAS
HERE.

648
00:24:35,841 --> 00:24:36,842
I FEEL QUEASY.

649
00:24:36,842 --> 00:24:37,977
MY KNEES START
TO SHAKE,

650
00:24:37,977 --> 00:24:40,512
AND I JUST WANT TO TALK
TO MY DAD.

651
00:24:40,512 --> 00:24:41,513
(sobbing)

652
00:24:41,513 --> 00:24:43,115
I'M SCARED OF
HEIGHTS, DAD.

653
00:24:43,115 --> 00:24:44,717
I WISH YOU
COULD BE HERE.

654
00:24:48,020 --> 00:24:49,021
Man: WE'RE READY TO GO.

655
00:24:49,888 --> 00:24:53,459
NOW YOU CAN HOLD ON TO THE
CABLE WITH YOUR HANDS.

656
00:24:53,459 --> 00:24:57,329
April:
I FEEL LIKE MARY
POPPINS. WHOO!

657
00:24:57,329 --> 00:24:58,397
Richard: YEAH, YEAH!

658
00:25:01,734 --> 00:25:02,701
GO WITH THE SWING.

659
00:25:02,701 --> 00:25:04,937
THAT LOOKS COOL.

660
00:25:04,937 --> 00:25:05,938
THAT'S COOL.

661
00:25:05,938 --> 00:25:07,239
YEAH, YEAH,
YEAH, YEAH, YEAH!

662
00:25:07,239 --> 00:25:08,273
APRIL--SHE HAD NO FEAR,

663
00:25:08,273 --> 00:25:09,575
JUMPED RIGHT OUT
THERE.

664
00:25:09,575 --> 00:25:10,509
NOT THAT FAR. RIGHT.

665
00:25:13,712 --> 00:25:14,713
Shandi: WHOA.

666
00:25:14,713 --> 00:25:15,714
THAT'S REALLY
FAR DOWN.

667
00:25:15,714 --> 00:25:16,715
Richard: IN AND UP A LITTLE.

668
00:25:16,715 --> 00:25:17,716
YEAH, THERE
YOU GO.

669
00:25:17,716 --> 00:25:18,717
THAT WAY.
THAT WAY.

670
00:25:18,717 --> 00:25:19,718
THERE YOU GO.

671
00:25:19,718 --> 00:25:20,719
Jay: THAT'S GREAT.

672
00:25:20,719 --> 00:25:21,854
Richard:
SHANDI--SHE GAVE

673
00:25:21,854 --> 00:25:24,556
A TREMENDOUS
RANGE OF LOOKS, VERY SUBTLE,

674
00:25:24,556 --> 00:25:25,624
BUT DIFFERENT,

675
00:25:25,624 --> 00:25:27,659
SO I WAS IMPRESSED BY
WHAT SHE DID.

676
00:25:27,659 --> 00:25:29,461
Sara: AAH! (laughing)

677
00:25:29,461 --> 00:25:31,230
OH, MY GOD!

678
00:25:31,230 --> 00:25:32,631
OH, MY GOD.

679
00:25:32,631 --> 00:25:33,632
Jay: YOUR RIGHT ARM,

680
00:25:33,632 --> 00:25:34,867
JUST STICK IT OUT.

681
00:25:34,867 --> 00:25:36,201
I KNOW IT'S DIFFICULT. VERY
DIFFICULT, RIGHT?

682
00:25:36,201 --> 00:25:39,371
SARA--SHE WAS TRYING TO
CONCENTRATE ON HER BODY

683
00:25:39,371 --> 00:25:41,874
SO MUCH THAT
SHE TOTALLY FORGOT

684
00:25:41,874 --> 00:25:43,308
WHAT WAS GOING ON FACIALLY.

685
00:25:43,308 --> 00:25:44,977
Richard: PULL YOURSELF FORWARD.

686
00:25:44,977 --> 00:25:47,212
DON'T LOOK AT ME
EVERY TIME, EITHER.

687
00:25:47,212 --> 00:25:48,981
Yoanna: I WANT TO HAVE
BABIES--BE CAREFUL.

688
00:25:48,981 --> 00:25:50,282
CAN I LET GO?

689
00:25:50,282 --> 00:25:51,750
Man: YEAH.

690
00:25:51,750 --> 00:25:53,819
Yoanna: OKAY, LETTING
GO. ALL RIGHT.

691
00:25:53,819 --> 00:25:55,087
Jay: BODY LANGUAGE IS PERFECT.

692
00:25:55,087 --> 00:25:57,489
I'M JUST TRYING TO GET
THE RIGHT HEAD THAT'S ALL.

693
00:25:57,489 --> 00:25:58,624
Man: LEFT ARM FORWARD.

694
00:25:58,624 --> 00:25:59,792
Jay: YOANNA, TRY AND HOLD THE
INTENSITY.

695
00:25:59,792 --> 00:26:01,026
LIKE, JUST FOCUS IT.

696
00:26:01,026 --> 00:26:02,261
YOANNA WAS
REALLY SCATTERED.

697
00:26:02,261 --> 00:26:03,729
I FELT LIKE I
HAD TO STRUGGLE

698
00:26:03,729 --> 00:26:05,564
TO GET HER TO FOCUS.

699
00:26:05,564 --> 00:26:06,965
THERE YOU GO.

700
00:26:06,965 --> 00:26:12,171
♪♪♪

701
00:26:12,171 --> 00:26:14,807
Heather: THIS CAN HURT CATIE
DURING ELIMINATION 'CAUSE

702
00:26:14,807 --> 00:26:16,308
IF SHE
